<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nevada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nevada is a state in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, largely within the arid Great Basin, with its capital at Carson City. Acquired from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1848 and first part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah-territory">Utah Territory</a>, it boomed after the discovery of the Comstock Lode <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> deposits in 1859 and was admitted as a state in 1864, during the Civil War. In the twentieth century legal gambling made Las Vegas and Reno famous.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nevada.jpg" alt="Nevada" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Caleb Moore · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nevada.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Ghost Dance songs belong to a ceremony that began among the Northern Paiute of Mason Valley, in what became the state of <b>Nevada</b>.</blockquote><a href="/songs/ghost-dance">Ghost Dance songs</a></li><li><blockquote>Mexico ceded about half its territory, including California, <b>Nevada</b>, Utah and most of Arizona and New Mexico, to the United States for 15 million dollars, and recognised Texas as American.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/february-2">2 February in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Two days before leaving office, President James Buchanan signed acts organising the <b>Nevada</b> and Dakota territories.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-2">2 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote>An Act of Congress established Yosemite National Park in California's Sierra <b>Nevada</b>, protecting the high country around the Yosemite Valley.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-1">1 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Nevada</b> was admitted to the Union during the Civil War, with Republicans keen on its votes for Lincoln's re-election and support for the 13th Amendment.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-31">31 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Deseret claimed a huge area covering most of present-day Utah and <b>Nevada</b>, much of Arizona and parts of six other states, with a corridor to the Pacific at San Diego.</blockquote><a href="/state/state-of-deseret">State of Deseret</a></li></ul></section>
